    "chunk_size_bytes": 1567,
    "chunk_text": "The Atrophied Wife\n\nMTL Ebell is a well-known, established Sri Lankan writer, who has authored many publications winning the State Literary Award in 2008 for best short stories in English titled Short and Verse and in 2014 for the best English novel Thus She Grew.\n\nHer latest publication, The Atrophied Wife, a piece of writing that takes the reader on an emotional roller coaster, should be on the list of \u2018must read\u2019 books of every discerning reader. The story does not just \u2018begin\u2019 but erupts from the very first word, and grabs your attention with a vice-like grip.\n\nThis book is worked within the framework of a traditional novel, a family saga spanning generations. Yet, it explodes with modernity in the sense that it explores subjects that the good old-fashioned novelist did not dare to touch.\n\nEbell delves into relationships with sensitivity and a deep understanding of the human condition laying bare a perspective of humanity which falls outside accepted societal norms; aspects that society would rather \u2018sweep under the carpet\u2019 and some would even look upon as sinful. However, reality must be accepted and truth be told, and the writer tells it.\n\nShe explores abusive and loving relationships, issues of child development, moral dilemmas, internal conflicts, sexuality, and sexual deviance. She does it with calm acceptance of reality. Yes, shocking maybe, but never crude. Sometimes deep dark subterranean feelings are also alluded to but not fully exposed; the author half opens up the \u2018can of worms\u2019 allowing the reader to peer in."
  },
