    "date_str": "2025-12-23",
    "description": "Public-private partnerships strengthen rebuilding efforts post-Cyclone Ditwah",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Public-private-partnerships-strengthen-rebuilding-efforts-post-Cyclone-Ditwah/34-785992",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1766439053.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-23-dailyftlk-8ae90f7c-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8e4b77be6efd1e52ecd024a7a4814ac1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1321,
    "chunk_text": "Public-private partnerships strengthen rebuilding efforts post-Cyclone Ditwah\n\nSecretary to the President Dr. Nandika Sanath Kumanayake (right)\u00a0receiving a cheque of Rs. 50 million for flood relief and humanitarian efforts from Pyramid Wilmar Group Managing Director M. Sajjad Mawzoon (centre) and Director/Chief Operating Officer Thanveer Siddique\n\nPyramid Wilmar donates Rs. 50 m for flood and landslide relief\n\nPyramid Wilmar, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most progressive and influential corporate entities in the food manufacturing and marketing sector has donated a sum of Rs. 50 million to the Presidential Secretariat to aid the Government\u2019s relief effort towards the victims of the recent Ditwah cyclone.\n\nPyramid Wilmar Ltd. Group Managing Director M. Sajjad Mawzoon said, \u201cThe devastation that took place throughout the country due to the recent cyclone has left everyone in a vulnerable situation. For some who lost their loved ones, life will not be the same. In light of all affected individuals and families, we stand with the people of Sri Lanka as the country begins to recover and rebuild from this existential challenge. Our commitment is to change life for the better.\u201d\n\nPyramid Wilmar remains committed to its mandate for social responsibility, ensuring support for communities during times of crisis."
  },
